Give the two load-sensitive federation tests a 30s timeout (up from the 10s
default) so a slow-but-healthy run under full-suite load does not trip the
sytest test deadline.

Both tests wait on federation delivery that the sytest suite exercises while
sharing the runner with the parallel Complement/Crypto jobs and the second
monolith process:

- "Can recv device messages over federation" waits for an m.direct_to_device
  EDU to round-trip between the two monoliths.
- "Presence changes to UNAVAILABLE are reported to remote room members" waits
  for a remote user to receive an m.presence EDU.

Each test genuinely passes on a clean run (see the baseline and the sytest
job's retry), but under load the 10s default deadline is occasionally too
tight. A real regression still fails within 30s.

If this stops applying against a newer sytest develop, rebase it (the hunks
are in stable, old test code).

--- a/tests/46direct/04federation.pl
+++ b/tests/46direct/04federation.pl
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 test "Can recv device messages over federation",
+   timeout => 30,
    requires => [ local_user_fixture(), remote_user_fixture(),
       qw( can_recv_device_message ) ],
 
--- a/tests/40presence.pl
+++ b/tests/40presence.pl
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@
    };
 
 test "Presence changes to UNAVAILABLE are reported to remote room members",
+   timeout => 30,
    requires => [ $senduser_fixture, $remote_user_fixture, $room_fixture,
                  qw( can_set_presence can_join_remote_room_by_alias )],
